Package: StateSpaceSIR
Type: Package
Title: State-Space Surplus Production Models Fitted by Sampling-Importance-Resampling
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Grant", "Adams", email = "adamsgd@uw.edu", role = c("cre", "aut")),
    person("John", "Best", email = "jkbest@gmail.com", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits Bayesian state-space generalized logistic (surplus production)
    models using the sampling-importance-resampling (SIR) algorithm of
    McAllister et al. (1994), following Zerbini et al. (2011, 2019) and Romero
    et al. (2022). Combines catch series with absolute and relative abundance
    indices, supports multivariate lognormal index likelihoods with analytically
    integrated catchability, and provides four parameterisations of a
    demographic Allee effect (depensation). Includes model averaging by Bayes
    factor, WAIC, and plotting and summary methods. Developed for southern right
    whales (Eubalaena australis) in the southwestern Atlantic Ocean but
    applicable to other depleted populations.
